    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (73.12) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.07) leading the charge as our most potent assets. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite the left-on-left matchup against Kendry Rojas; his elite 0.425 xwOBA and the favorable 5.83 xERA of the opposing starter override the platoon disadvantage. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits immensely from the wind-aided park conditions and a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Brandon Sproat, providing a high-ceiling play that maximizes our scoring potential despite his projected spot in the lower third of the batting order. **Trea Turner** (71.38) and **Kyle Schwarber** (69.17) round out the top tier, with both players gaining significant value from their premier order slots and wind-supported conditions against Nick Lodolo.\n\nStrategic roster construction today favors aggressive placement over purely raw output, exemplified by our decision to hold **Luke Raley** (48.62) on the bench. While **Luke Raley** offers a strong score relative to his base, he was nudged out of the UTIL spot by **Junior Caminero** (57.62); while **Junior Caminero** faces a tougher matchup against Trevor Rogers, the optimizer prioritized the higher projected efficiency and order placement. **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith** remain high-leverage plays, though their outlook is tempered by a 41% rain risk in their matchup against Slade Cecconi. We are closely monitoring weather reports, as any further degradation in conditions could force a pivot away from this stack to preserve our remaining game caps for more stable environments.",
